---
title: "SD-02 Clone / Fetch over Smart HTTP (UML Sequence Diagram)"
---
sequenceDiagram
  autonumber
  actor C as git client
  participant H as smarthttp.Handler
  participant A as auth.Service
  participant R as repos.Service
  participant Z as auth.Authorizer
  participant G as git upload-pack (process)

  C->>H: GET /alice/demo.git/info/refs?service=git-upload-pack
  H->>A: ActorFromRequest(r)
  A-->>H: Actor (anonymous or user)
  H->>R: resolve alice/demo
  H->>Z: Require(actor, repo, Read)
  alt private repo and anonymous
    Z-->>H: errs.NotFound
    H-->>C: 401 WWW-Authenticate: Basic
    C->>H: retry with Authorization: Basic user:PAT
  end
  H->>G: spawn upload-pack --stateless-rpc --advertise-refs (GIT_PROTOCOL from header)
  G-->>H: ref advertisement
  H-->>C: 200 application/x-git-upload-pack-advertisement
  C->>H: POST /alice/demo.git/git-upload-pack (wants / haves)
  H->>G: spawn upload-pack --stateless-rpc, pipe body to stdin
  loop stream
    G-->>H: packfile bytes
    H-->>C: packfile bytes (no buffering)
  end
  Note over H,G: if the client disconnects, ctx is cancelled and the git process is killed
